  "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes this user report on `requesty codex`:\n\n```\nError loading config.toml: model_providers.requesty: provider auth cannot be combined with env_key\n```\n\nA hand-written `[model_providers.requesty]` can set `env_key = \"OPENAI_API_KEY\"`, which is what our Codex docs describe. Our `auth.command` then lands on that same table and Codex refuses it. Codex also refuses `auth` combined with `experimental_bearer_token` or `requires_openai_auth`. This happens both when the `-c` overrides from `requesty codex` are merged in and when `requesty configure` merges into the file.\n\n`[model_providers.requesty]` is our own section, so `configureMerge` now deletes those three keys from it after merging:\n\n```go\ndelete(config[\"model_providers\"][\"requesty\"], \"env_key\" | \"experimental_bearer_token\" | \"requires_openai_auth\")\n```\n\nEverything else is still merged, and the file is still backed up first.\n\n`Launch` is unchanged and writes nothing to disk. A user who only runs `requesty codex` without re-configuring will still see the error until they run configure, or remove the key by hand.\n\nTest added: `TestCodexHarnessConfigureMergeDropsConflictingProviderAuth`\n\nLink to Devin session: https://app.devin.ai/sessions/c3f712f027814498ab963003b0d22e9a\nOpen in Devin Desktop: https://app.devin.ai/desktop/session/c3f712f027814498ab963003b0d22e9a?variant=devin",
